The retrieved candidates did not come with the question they were retrieved for, so this answer summarizes the factual evidence they contain. Four of the ten candidates were exact duplicates and were merged.

1. **SearchFlow System Design Document.** eid_95f6d01c shared the System Design Document for SearchFlow in #planning-SearchFlow and asked for feedback (source 20260319-0-e74ad, 2026-03-19). The same person later posted the updated, final version and thanked the team (source 20260322-0-8cdf6, 2026-03-22). The 2026-03-22 version is the more recent one and should be treated as the current document.

2. **Planned revisions to the product/PM document.** In #planning-SearchFlow-PM, eid_1f678d18 summarized five agreed changes (source 20260226-6-33552, 2026-02-26):
   - add examples of the AI capabilities to the Product Differentiation section;
   - say how user feedback will be gathered in Product Development;
   - add data on Slack's search limitations to Market Opportunity;
   - describe industry events and testimonial strategies in Go-to-Market;
   - mention the initial beta feedback.

3. **Customization limits.** eid_3bcf2a20 told Ian that SearchFlow's customization is "quite basic." Users can't build complex search queries or adjust filters beyond a few preset options, which could limit teams with specific search needs (source 20260522-4-8735a, 2026-05-22).

4. **Bug fix PR.** In #bug-georgebrown-SearchFlow, eid_a4fa6150 pointed to the changes in PR https://github.com/salesforce/SearchFlow/pull/58 (source 20261027-3-653ac, 2026-10-27).

5. **Product name.** eid_e96d2f38 agreed that the name "SearchFlow" captures the essence of the product better and called it a strong move (source 20260316-2-b37a5, 2026-03-16). The candidates don't say what the earlier name was.
